01:50:03.790 --> 01:50:05.727
he's at the deep end again,
jumps in, drowns again.

01:50:05.727 --> 01:50:07.037
I have to go in and get him.

01:50:07.037 --> 01:50:09.470
And tell his parents off, and
his parents have a go at me

01:50:09.470 --> 01:50:10.920
and complained to my manager saying that

01:50:10.920 --> 01:50:13.710
it's not my place to tell
her what to teach her kids.

01:50:13.710 --> 01:50:16.439
And I'm like, it's not my place.

01:50:16.439 --> 01:50:17.830
I can just let your kid drown, huh?

01:50:17.830 --> 01:50:18.821
See what happens.

01:50:18.821 --> 01:50:20.290
- What the fuck?
- She went full Karen mode

01:50:20.290 --> 01:50:21.820
on me, trying to get me fired.

01:50:21.820 --> 01:50:23.660
'cause I bollocked her in front of her-

01:50:23.660 --> 01:50:26.220
- What, because you saved their kid?

01:50:26.220 --> 01:50:28.330
- After I saved his kid twice,

01:50:28.330 --> 01:50:30.930
I held his hand and I was
like, come, where's your mom?

01:50:30.930 --> 01:50:31.870
Show me where your mom is?

01:50:31.870 --> 01:50:33.190
And then we went to his mom.

01:50:33.190 --> 01:50:34.023
- Where's your mom. (claps)

01:50:34.023 --> 01:50:35.312
- I was like,

01:50:35.312 --> 01:50:36.262
what are you doing?
- What are you doing?

01:50:36.262 --> 01:50:37.095
(laughing)

01:50:37.095 --> 01:50:39.510
- I was like why are you
letting this kid into this pool

01:50:39.510 --> 01:50:41.170
without any arm bands or anything?

01:50:41.170 --> 01:50:42.003
- And she's like, oh-
- Like didn't have

01:50:42.003 --> 01:50:43.726
any floaties or anything.

01:50:43.726 --> 01:50:44.559
- That's a (indistinct).

01:50:44.559 --> 01:50:45.392
Why didn't they have armbands?

01:50:45.392 --> 01:50:46.450
- You know what her reason was?

01:50:46.450 --> 01:50:47.820
She was like, I don't want him to feel

01:50:47.820 --> 01:50:51.708
like he's the weird one,
the one who can't swim.

01:50:51.708 --> 01:50:52.673
And I'm like-

01:50:52.673 --> 01:50:54.200
- But he's the one who can't swim.

01:50:54.200 --> 01:50:55.290
- That's because he can't swim.

01:50:55.290 --> 01:50:56.960
He will fucking drown.

01:50:56.960 --> 01:50:59.050
Do you understand how this works?

01:50:59.050 --> 01:51:00.937
I'm like, did you ever
teach him how to swim?

01:51:00.937 --> 01:51:01.780
"No."

01:51:01.780 --> 01:51:02.613
Why are you letting him do this?

01:51:02.613 --> 01:51:04.240
This is really irresponsible.

01:51:04.240 --> 01:51:05.073
And then I just left.

01:51:05.073 --> 01:51:06.550
And this was in front of all her friends,

01:51:06.550 --> 01:51:08.010
'cause they had like a (indistinct)

01:51:08.010 --> 01:51:09.020
And then she complained saying,

01:51:09.020 --> 01:51:10.820
I didn't need to do that in
front of all her friends.

01:51:10.820 --> 01:51:12.190
It was really inappropriate of me.

01:51:12.190 --> 01:51:15.830
I'm like, I'm sorry, but
you saw your kid drown once

01:51:15.830 --> 01:51:18.630
and thought, "Oh, I'll
let him keep swimming.

01:51:18.630 --> 01:51:19.463
I let him keep going."

01:51:19.463 --> 01:51:20.296
That really me off.

01:51:20.296 --> 01:51:21.140
I'm still really annoyed about that.

01:51:21.140 --> 01:51:23.083
- Yeah, that's just fucking irresponsible.

01:51:23.083 --> 01:51:25.030
- That just sounds like bad parenting.

01:51:25.030 --> 01:51:26.190
- Yeah, it's terrible parenting.

01:51:26.190 --> 01:51:27.480
The people who do stuff
like they would just let

01:51:27.480 --> 01:51:28.313
their kids do-

01:51:28.313 --> 01:51:29.930
- Unless the parent was
like, "Fuck, I've been trying

01:51:29.930 --> 01:51:30.883
to get rid of him."

01:51:30.883 --> 01:51:32.286
(laughing)

01:51:32.286 --> 01:51:34.100
- The fuck!
- Sabotaged again.

01:51:34.100 --> 01:51:35.230
- That insurance plan.

01:51:35.230 --> 01:51:37.230
Damn, its really expensive monthly.

01:51:37.230 --> 01:51:38.667
- That's a really lay abortion plan.

01:51:38.667 --> 01:51:40.000
(laughs)

01:51:40.000 --> 01:51:41.080
- [Meilyne] We have it in Japan.

01:51:41.080 --> 01:51:42.520
- Do they? Wow!

01:51:42.520 --> 01:51:43.430
- Oh my God! Look at that.

01:51:43.430 --> 01:51:45.040
- Oh, that looks amazing.

01:51:45.040 --> 01:51:46.480
Can you send that
picture when you're done.

01:51:46.480 --> 01:51:47.620
- Get ready. Next special.

01:51:47.620 --> 01:51:48.453
Were fucking doing it.

01:51:48.453 --> 01:51:50.280
- Doesn't this look amazing?

01:51:50.280 --> 01:51:51.113
- Fucking hell.

01:51:51.113 --> 01:51:52.983
- Dude, it was a really
good job other than that.

01:51:52.983 --> 01:51:55.480
It's just like kids that just
like don't know how to swim

01:51:55.480 --> 01:51:57.100
and you can tell a moment they can't swim.

01:51:57.100 --> 01:51:58.400
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:51:58.400 --> 01:52:00.910
- And yeah, also if you ever tried to,

01:52:00.910 --> 01:52:02.367
sometimes if you'd, they taught you

01:52:02.367 --> 01:52:04.350
and I never thought I'd have to use this.

01:52:04.350 --> 01:52:06.605
They teach you how to
kick someone off you.

01:52:06.605 --> 01:52:10.595
if they're like trying to drag you down.

01:52:10.595 --> 01:52:12.880
- If you're trying to save someone, right?

01:52:12.880 --> 01:52:14.420
- Don't drag me, you're coming with me.

01:52:14.420 --> 01:52:17.020
- 'Cause some people when
they think their drowning

01:52:17.020 --> 01:52:19.620
they panic, and what they do
is that they push you down.

01:52:19.620 --> 01:52:20.720
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Cause they think,

01:52:20.720 --> 01:52:21.560
I wanna get up.

01:52:21.560 --> 01:52:23.210
And, you know, it's not
like a selfish thing

01:52:23.210 --> 01:52:25.353
where they're like, "Fuck you."

01:52:25.353 --> 01:52:28.650
- I'm dying and you're
dying with me. (laughs)

01:52:28.650 --> 01:52:30.710
- Yeah literally, it's like
instincts kick in for them

01:52:30.710 --> 01:52:33.570
and they think I'm gonna
push you down to get up

01:52:33.570 --> 01:52:34.840
so I can breath.

01:52:34.840 --> 01:52:35.673
- What was the technique?

01:52:35.673 --> 01:52:36.506
- So what you do is-

01:52:36.506 --> 01:52:37.420
- Just like aim for the head.

01:52:37.420 --> 01:52:39.186
- No.
( laughing)

01:52:39.186 --> 01:52:42.063
(indistinct)

01:52:42.063 --> 01:52:44.040
So if they're trying
to like grab on to you

01:52:44.040 --> 01:52:47.053
and push you down, you grab
them by the arms and like,

01:52:48.150 --> 01:52:50.090
so let's say you're
equal now in the water,

01:52:50.090 --> 01:52:51.550
we're both on top of the (indistinct).

01:52:51.550 --> 01:52:54.390
You grab them and like you
go down under the water,

01:52:54.390 --> 01:52:56.280
kick them up and kick them off you.

01:52:56.280 --> 01:52:57.670
- Right, right, right, right.

01:52:57.670 --> 01:52:58.880
- You push them away.

01:52:58.880 --> 01:53:02.492
And then you usually just grab
them by the face when you-

01:53:02.492 --> 01:53:03.380
- What are you doing?

01:53:03.380 --> 01:53:04.280
- I'm not kidding.

01:53:05.249 --> 01:53:06.082
When you save someone,

01:53:06.082 --> 01:53:08.340
you're supposed to grab
them by the chin like this

01:53:08.340 --> 01:53:09.520
and like pull them.

01:53:09.520 --> 01:53:10.918
- Holy shit!

01:53:10.918 --> 01:53:13.090
- Or you can, there's some other ways,

01:53:13.090 --> 01:53:13.923
but that's the easiest,

01:53:13.923 --> 01:53:16.610
'cause that way you can kinda
just do it at your own pace.

01:53:16.610 --> 01:53:18.570
There's other ways that you can grab them,

01:53:18.570 --> 01:53:20.230
but that's really awkward.

01:53:20.230 --> 01:53:21.737
It depends like how big they are.

01:53:21.737 --> 01:53:23.260
And if it's like a child,

01:53:23.260 --> 01:53:24.470
like sometimes grabbing them by the face

01:53:24.470 --> 01:53:25.306
might be a bit much.

01:53:25.306 --> 01:53:26.360
(laughs)

01:53:26.360 --> 01:53:27.193
Fuck! Get over here.

01:53:27.193 --> 01:53:28.054
- Get over here.

01:53:28.054 --> 01:53:30.126
(laughing)

01:53:30.126 --> 01:53:33.600
- I just imagine you like
you're wielding children,

01:53:33.600 --> 01:53:36.674
grabbing in the face. (groans)

01:53:36.674 --> 01:53:38.103
(roars)

01:53:38.103 --> 01:53:40.420
- You know the worst thing, when you...

01:53:40.420 --> 01:53:41.603
This is the thing that you
don't really think about

01:53:41.603 --> 01:53:43.560
is that you don't bring spare uniforms,

01:53:43.560 --> 01:53:44.510
'cause that's really your thing.

01:53:44.510 --> 01:53:48.050
So if you go in and you save a kid

01:53:48.050 --> 01:53:49.220
and it's still your shift,

01:53:49.220 --> 01:53:52.600
you just go right back to
the chair and you're soaking.

01:53:52.600 --> 01:53:55.060
And you know, some people
they take the time.

01:53:55.060 --> 01:53:56.370
Like the first time I did it,

01:53:56.370 --> 01:53:58.710
I thought I have to go in right away,

01:53:58.710 --> 01:54:00.690
I have to save that life right away.

01:54:00.690 --> 01:54:02.490
And I wouldn't take my
shoes off or anything,

01:54:02.490 --> 01:54:04.480
but then I realized all the
people who are experienced,

01:54:04.480 --> 01:54:06.040
they would just walk down slowly.

01:54:06.040 --> 01:54:08.170
They would just take off
their shoes and socks,

01:54:08.170 --> 01:54:09.187
'cause they knew they had time,

01:54:09.187 --> 01:54:10.530
and they knew like it's a pool.

01:54:10.530 --> 01:54:12.290
- They know they're gonna
grab them right away.

01:54:12.290 --> 01:54:14.230
So they're like, "I'm not
getting my Nike Air Maxes wet.

01:54:14.230 --> 01:54:15.138
What the fuck, bro.

01:54:15.138 --> 01:54:15.971
(laughing)

01:54:15.971 --> 01:54:18.545
- (indistinct) kid's
drowning and they kinda like

01:54:18.545 --> 01:54:19.690
start the timer.

01:54:19.690 --> 01:54:21.080
- They sit down like this, right?

01:54:21.080 --> 01:54:22.070
They see them like...

01:54:22.070 --> 01:54:23.630
'Cause if they're flailing,
you got plenty of time.

01:54:23.630 --> 01:54:25.300
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- So they would just sit.

01:54:25.300 --> 01:54:26.897
They'd like walk down
really slowly like this

01:54:26.897 --> 01:54:28.984
and they'd be like, "Okay."

01:54:28.984 --> 01:54:30.247
(laughing)

01:54:30.247 --> 01:54:32.747
Take the watch off like
this, you know, like that.

01:54:33.672 --> 01:54:35.670
Then they would go in to get them.

01:54:35.670 --> 01:54:36.503
It was really funny.

01:54:36.503 --> 01:54:38.457
I just thought it was really bizarre.

01:54:38.457 --> 01:54:39.290
I was like, why did you do that?

01:54:39.290 --> 01:54:40.202
Isn't that like bad?

01:54:40.202 --> 01:54:41.035
They're like, "No, no, no.

01:54:41.035 --> 01:54:42.490
They're not gonna drown.

01:54:42.490 --> 01:54:43.590
- They're not gonna drown

01:54:43.590 --> 01:54:46.650
- I know the average time it
takes for a human to drown.

01:54:46.650 --> 01:54:47.580
- Again, the moment I feel worried

01:54:47.580 --> 01:54:48.799
is if they don't come back up.

01:54:48.799 --> 01:54:50.646
That's when you have to
like immediately go in.

01:54:50.646 --> 01:54:51.960
So that was like, that was fine.

01:54:51.960 --> 01:54:53.570
And again, this like never happened ever.

01:54:53.570 --> 01:54:56.680
This was only with little kids,
'cause little kids are dumb.

01:54:56.680 --> 01:54:57.650
I mean, I make out these stories

01:54:57.650 --> 01:54:59.050
to be a lot more exciting than they are.

01:54:59.050 --> 01:55:01.410
In general, the job was extremely boring.

01:55:01.410 --> 01:55:04.120
Like it is one of the hardest jobs to do

01:55:04.120 --> 01:55:06.320
just out of sheer insanity.

01:55:06.320 --> 01:55:08.420
You sit there for 30 minutes at a time,

01:55:08.420 --> 01:55:10.070
just watching people swim.

01:55:10.070 --> 01:55:10.915
- Yeah.

01:55:10.915 --> 01:55:11.748
- Then you take a 20-minute break

01:55:11.748 --> 01:55:12.581
and then you'd go back to it,

01:55:12.581 --> 01:55:13.755
and this is like for like six hours.

01:55:13.755 --> 01:55:15.100
You're just watching people swim.

01:55:15.100 --> 01:55:16.257
And at first it's such
a weird thing to do,

01:55:16.257 --> 01:55:18.770
'cause I'm like, yo, what do
people get a problem with me

01:55:18.770 --> 01:55:21.399
like staring at them
while they're swimming?

01:55:21.399 --> 01:55:23.160
'Cause I'm like, you don't
stare at people (indistinct).

01:55:23.160 --> 01:55:24.440
But you're gonna watch the pool, right?

01:55:24.440 --> 01:55:25.364
But then you're like, fuck,

01:55:25.364 --> 01:55:26.320
is it weird that I'm looking at people,

01:55:26.320 --> 01:55:27.743
like there's Parents watching me.

01:55:27.743 --> 01:55:29.057
What if they think I'm
looking at their kid too much?

01:55:29.057 --> 01:55:30.780
But I'm just making sure that
they're not drowning, okay?

01:55:30.780 --> 01:55:33.940
It's not weird, right? (laughs)

01:55:33.940 --> 01:55:34.773
- Well, according to (indistinct)-

01:55:34.773 --> 01:55:37.560
I wasn't even thinking
about that until he said it.

01:55:37.560 --> 01:55:39.190
- This is the thing, these
are the thoughts you have

01:55:39.190 --> 01:55:40.210
when you're going insane

01:55:40.210 --> 01:55:42.420
sitting there for six hours
thinking like, is it weird?

01:55:42.420 --> 01:55:45.040
Is it weird that I'm looking
at everyone for this long?

01:55:45.040 --> 01:55:46.420
I'm going insane.
- Sounds like

01:55:46.420 --> 01:55:48.210
an existential crisis.

01:55:48.210 --> 01:55:49.400
What is my job?

01:55:49.400 --> 01:55:52.170
- I legitimately started like
going insane working there.

01:55:52.170 --> 01:55:54.208
'Cause I was like, you have to just think

01:55:54.208 --> 01:55:55.713
so much.
- How long did you do that?

01:55:56.720 --> 01:55:58.510
- God, about just under a year

01:55:59.732 --> 01:56:01.690
and then I moved away.

01:56:01.690 --> 01:56:03.300
But yeah, I got that job
from doing a different job,

01:56:03.300 --> 01:56:04.220
which I talked about at different times.

01:56:04.220 --> 01:56:06.807
Just completely different and
it was really funny as well.

01:56:06.807 --> 01:56:09.240
But like lifeguarding in general
it was like super boring,

01:56:09.240 --> 01:56:10.180
but the pay was really good

01:56:10.180 --> 01:56:11.910
'cause you have to get the qualification.

01:56:11.910 --> 01:56:14.630
And you have to be taught a lot of stuff.

01:56:14.630 --> 01:56:16.120
- Yeah you're there to save lives.

01:56:16.120 --> 01:56:18.120
- Yeah, yeah and the course is quite hard,

01:56:18.120 --> 01:56:19.790
and you have to redo it every year.

01:56:19.790 --> 01:56:22.520
And so I can't be a lifeguard
now 'cause I didn't renew it.

01:56:22.520 --> 01:56:23.520
- Oh, right, right.

01:56:23.520 --> 01:56:25.310
- But for the one year it was fine.

01:56:26.266 --> 01:56:27.930
I mean the pay was insane

01:56:27.930 --> 01:56:30.594
for like being 18 and (indistinct).

01:56:30.594 --> 01:56:33.310
- And I feel like learning
the basic first aid skills

01:56:33.310 --> 01:56:34.497
is really fucking important.
- Yeah, it was really helpful.

01:56:34.497 --> 01:56:36.925
- 'Cause I was never taught it at all.

01:56:36.925 --> 01:56:37.785
- We don't get taught in the UK.

01:56:37.785 --> 01:56:38.618
- Yeah, yeah, we don't get taught,

01:56:38.618 --> 01:56:40.330
so I don't know how to do CPR.

01:56:41.740 --> 01:56:44.330
They come in once and they're
like, push the chest and blow.

01:56:44.330 --> 01:56:45.163
- Oh we-

01:56:45.163 --> 01:56:46.290
- I didn't even get that.

01:56:46.290 --> 01:56:47.220
I didn't even get that.
- Oh, really?

01:56:47.220 --> 01:56:51.360
- We taught it every
year during high school.

01:56:51.360 --> 01:56:52.260
- I do not know how to do

01:56:52.260 --> 01:56:53.797
the fucking Heimlich maneuver only.

01:56:53.797 --> 01:56:55.204
- I need to learn that as well.

01:56:55.204 --> 01:56:56.037
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:56:56.037 --> 01:56:57.660
- We just have to learn all the basics-

01:56:58.972 --> 01:57:00.190
- I should probably learn it now

01:57:00.190 --> 01:57:02.550
because it's gonna be real
awkward if I'm gonna be like,

01:57:02.550 --> 01:57:04.520
hold on, let me just bring
up this YouTube tutorial

01:57:04.520 --> 01:57:05.650
for a second.

01:57:05.650 --> 01:57:06.483
All right, wait, wait,

01:57:06.483 --> 01:57:07.570
I got an unskippable ad.

01:57:07.570 --> 01:57:08.734
- It's sponsored. It's sponsored.

01:57:08.734 --> 01:57:10.040
- I've got an unskippable ad.

01:57:10.040 --> 01:57:12.298
Hold on a second. (laughs)

01:57:12.298 --> 01:57:15.024
- Wifi. Where's the Wifi?

01:57:15.024 --> 01:57:19.130
- A lot of aspects of the
job were fun, but not many.

01:57:19.130 --> 01:57:20.250
I had to like clean as well,

01:57:20.250 --> 01:57:22.930
like clean all the toilets and showers,

01:57:22.930 --> 01:57:25.540
which was like, I mean, I
didn't know I was gonna do that.

01:57:25.540 --> 01:57:27.806
- Glad you spent 400
bucks to clean toilets.

01:57:27.806 --> 01:57:29.465
(indistinct)

01:57:29.465 --> 01:57:30.520
Fucking hell.

01:57:30.520 --> 01:57:33.140
- You know, you're there
and when you're wrapping up

01:57:33.140 --> 01:57:34.500
and there's no one left in the pool,

01:57:34.500 --> 01:57:35.333
you just start cleaning

01:57:35.333 --> 01:57:38.070
'cause that's what you're
supposed to do, but yeah.

01:57:38.070 --> 01:57:40.740
And then sometimes I had to like,

01:57:40.740 --> 01:57:42.760
'cause even though I
wasn't teaching the kids,

01:57:42.760 --> 01:57:45.650
but for the kids who
are like one year old,

01:57:45.650 --> 01:57:46.483
they're learning how to swim,

01:57:46.483 --> 01:57:48.810
there had to be someone in the
water constantly with them.

01:57:48.810 --> 01:57:49.643
- Right. Right.

01:57:49.643 --> 01:57:51.890
- And those kids just fucking
like don't let go of you.

01:57:51.890 --> 01:57:53.240
And it's like, no, get
off me you little shit

01:57:53.240 --> 01:57:54.880
It's like WrestleMania with like babies.

01:57:54.880 --> 01:57:56.000
It's like, get off me.

01:57:56.000 --> 01:57:57.250
You're supposed to learn how to swim.

01:57:57.250 --> 01:57:59.536
- But the moment they let
go of the wall they're like.

01:57:59.536 --> 01:58:01.510
And they suddenly gained the grip strength

01:58:01.510 --> 01:58:02.843
of like a grown man.

01:58:03.935 --> 01:58:04.768
It was just, yeah.

01:58:04.768 --> 01:58:06.663
I mean, it was all right job, really?

01:58:06.663 --> 01:58:08.027
It just paid well, but-

01:58:08.027 --> 01:58:09.393
- The kids at the pool were scary.

01:58:09.393 --> 01:58:10.473
