02:01:33.190 --> 02:01:35.030
if you're getting even like 1% tired,

02:01:35.030 --> 02:01:35.863
like you should turn back.

02:01:35.863 --> 02:01:37.559
- Yeah, I was already pretty tired.

02:01:37.559 --> 02:01:38.392
- You should turn the fuck around.

02:01:38.392 --> 02:01:39.225
- That's how people drown.

02:01:39.225 --> 02:01:40.460
- That's probably like the closest

02:01:40.460 --> 02:01:42.750
I've come to drowning as well.

02:01:42.750 --> 02:01:44.150
- People get tired and they swim out

02:01:44.150 --> 02:01:44.983
and then they're like,

02:01:44.983 --> 02:01:46.915
they're tired by the time they turn around

02:01:46.915 --> 02:01:47.748
and they're fucked.

02:01:47.748 --> 02:01:48.581
It's so sad.

02:01:48.581 --> 02:01:53.010
- And yeah, I remember turning
around and being like, okay,

02:01:53.010 --> 02:01:56.390
I've gotta fucking do this
because one of the scariest-

02:01:56.390 --> 02:01:57.550
- My life literally depends on it.

02:01:57.550 --> 02:01:58.820
- My life literally depends on it.

02:01:58.820 --> 02:02:02.230
And I was like, guys, I
think I gotta turn back.

02:02:02.230 --> 02:02:04.960
And I don't think I kind of conveyed

02:02:04.960 --> 02:02:07.810
how fucking terrified I was to my mates,

02:02:07.810 --> 02:02:09.790
'cause they were like,
"We're just gonna keep going

02:02:09.790 --> 02:02:10.623
if that's cool with you."

02:02:10.623 --> 02:02:12.990
And I'm like, (pants) okay, okay.

02:02:12.990 --> 02:02:14.660
I'm gonna turn back now.

02:02:14.660 --> 02:02:15.493
So yeah.

02:02:15.493 --> 02:02:17.479
- What a great group of friends-

02:02:17.479 --> 02:02:20.890
- Those are bad mates
if they let you do that.

02:02:20.890 --> 02:02:23.360
- I mean, I didn't have
a good group of mates

02:02:23.360 --> 02:02:24.193
when I was growing up.

02:02:24.193 --> 02:02:25.870
- If I heard even like
a breath from my friend

02:02:25.870 --> 02:02:27.490
that sounded a little too
heavy and we're swimming,

02:02:27.490 --> 02:02:30.363
I'm like, turn the fuck
around and get the fuck back.

02:02:30.363 --> 02:02:31.254
- Fucking hell.

02:02:31.254 --> 02:02:32.954
- 'Cause when you get further
out, the waves get stronger.

02:02:32.954 --> 02:02:33.960
- Yeah, exactly.

02:02:33.960 --> 02:02:35.560
And then the currents come in

02:02:35.560 --> 02:02:37.600
and that's when it gets
really fucking scary.

02:02:37.600 --> 02:02:39.410
I mean, I can't think of
anything more depressing

02:02:39.410 --> 02:02:42.570
than just dying on
(indistinct) beach as well.

02:02:42.570 --> 02:02:44.260
At least if I'm gonna die on a beach,

02:02:44.260 --> 02:02:45.234
